{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make all UK Government websites free to access without mobile data charges",
        "additional_details": "People should not have to pay for mobile data to claim benefits, use health services, find safety advice, apply for work or understand their rights. Ofcom estimates that 3.8% of UK adults rely on mobile data alone and 0.9% rely only on external connections. New Zealand\u2019s Zero Data service shows a practical model: participating networks provide free access to government sites, with sponsoring agencies covering the data cost. Public services should be free at the point of access.",
        "background": "Require mobile network operators to zero-rate all UK Government websites and online services, so they never use a person\u2019s data allowance or require paid data. The Government should work with Ofcom and operators, cover delivery costs and include linked content needed to complete a service.",
        "closed_at": null,
